#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:1
msgid "ADR-0014: Operation mode, LumosLabs equipment and the digital twin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P12.1 to P12.10 (REQ-HW-1 to REQ-HW-8, REQ-EL-7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:9
msgid ""
"In operation mode the actions of elements are sent to real equipment "
"(ADR-0006, step P5.6 gave the `Driver` interface and `SimulatedDriver`). "
"Phase 12 must make this path safe and testable without hardware: bounds, "
"emergency stop, dry-run, confirmations, timeouts and recovery (REQ-HW-4),"
" transports (serial, TCP, VISA), a reference family of virtual devices, "
"LumosLabs, whose emulators speak a documented protocol over a real "
"transport (REQ-HW-3), discovery, the digital twin with real and simulated"
" outputs side by side (REQ-EL-7) and recorded sequences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:16
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:18
msgid ""
"**Package** `lumos.hardware`: `transport` (`Transport` with "
"`TCPTransport`, `SerialTransport` on pyserial URLs, including `loop://` "
"and `socket://`, `VisaTransport` on pyvisa, and an in-process "
"`PipeTransport`), `protocol` (the LumosLabs ASCII protocol), `emulators` "
"(one class per device and a threaded TCP server), `drivers` (one driver "
"per device, plus the plugin registry), `discovery`, `twin` and "
"`sequence`. pyserial and pyvisa stay optional (extra `[hardware]`); TCP "
"and pipes need nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:23
msgid ""
"**Driver safety in the base class**, so that every driver gets it: "
"software limits checked in `send` for every command, including commands "
"sent directly to the driver; `dry_run` validates and logs without "
"sending; actions listed as dangerous need a confirmation callback "
"(refused when absent); timeouts and a bounded number of reconnections on "
"transport errors; `stop()` usable from another thread, interrupting a "
"wait in progress; `safe_state()` (laser off, shutter closed, motion "
"stopped). `Context.stop_all()` stops every driver, and "
"`Context.operation_guard()` brings every driver to its safe state on "
"`KeyboardInterrupt` or any exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:29
msgid ""
"**Protocol**: one ASCII line per command and per reply, `\\n`-terminated;"
" replies `OK [value [unit]]` or `ERR <code> <message>`; common commands "
"`*IDN?`, `*RST`, `STATUS?`, `BUSY?`, `STOP`, `LIMITS? <name>`; quantities"
" always carry their unit. Long operations (moves, exposures) return at "
"once and are followed by `BUSY?` polling, which lets `STOP` interrupt "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:33
msgid ""
"**Emulators** run in-process (tests, notebooks) or as TCP servers (`lumos"
" emulators start`). They model latencies, noise, limits, homing, drifts "
"and **fault injection** (disconnection, delay, out-of-range value, stuck "
"motion). `LL-CAM` and `LL-PM` measure what the twin sends them through "
"`SIM:` commands of the protocol (`SIM:POWER`, `SIM:IMAGE`), then add "
"their own noise and defects: the real and simulated outputs then differ "
"in a controlled way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:38
msgid ""
"**Lab elements** (`lumos.elements.lab`): stages, piezo controller, "
"shutter, filter wheel, laser source, phase controller; "
"`ctx.link(\"stage.position\", \"gap.distance\", offset=...)` lets an "
"actuator drive a parameter of the optical model, so that the twin follows"
" the bench."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:41
msgid ""
"**Twin outputs**: in operation, detectors attached to a driver return the"
" measured `DataProduct`; the result of `ctx.run` also holds the simulated"
" outputs (`result.twin`) and the residuals (`result.residuals`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:43
msgid ""
"**Sequences**: `ctx.record()` records the actions as commands with their "
"arguments; a sequence replays in any mode and its commands are identical "
"in simulation and in operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:45
msgid ""
"**Plugins**: drivers of other packages register through the "
"`lumos.drivers` entry points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:47
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:49
msgid ""
"Driving the emulators by direct method calls: simpler, but the drivers "
"would not go through transports, errors and latencies (REQ-HW-3 requires "
"the same code path as real equipment)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:51
msgid ""
"asyncio drivers: the rest of LUMOS is synchronous; threads (a stop from "
"another thread, a polling loop) are enough for the bench equipment "
"considered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:53
msgid ""
"SCPI as the protocol: close in spirit, but its full grammar is much "
"larger than needed; the LumosLabs protocol borrows `*IDN?`/`*RST` and "
"keeps units explicit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:56
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:58
msgid ""
"Every new driver inherits the safety mechanisms; the emulators double as "
"the reference implementation of the protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:60
msgid ""
"The notebook `10_bench_operation` and the tests run against the emulators"
" without hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0014-operation-and-lumoslabs.md:61
msgid ""
"Vendor drivers (Thorlabs first) follow the same interface; the coverage "
"of their SDKs is documented."
msgstr ""

